   "from": "4a0dc082893a99c5",
   "note": "pro football screens use its own words (franchise, division, rank, the rankings) instead of college football's; only screen fingerprints change"
  },
  {
   "fp": "fd6507e2a2507647",
   "from": "e63438be654c1076",
   "note": "clinch marks (z/y/x/e) on standings, power ranking and playoff picture, and clinch lines in the stakes; standings show division record and mark the division leader. Only screen fingerprints change."
  },
  {
   "fp": "8490002e73885e9e",
   "from": "fd6507e2a2507647",
   "note": "standings sorted by overall record, then division record, the seeding order; note says so. Only screen fingerprints change."
  },
  {
   "fp": "60ead5ec273d3b91",
   "from": "8490002e73885e9e",
   "note": "People are fired on their grades: two missed seasons in a row at the same job (grade line 'Short of the mark' or worse), never one; the carousel no longer judges or poaches human coaches, and can't fill a fired user's job before they're told. History entries record miss. Carousel random draws for human-coached teams are gone, so careers diverge from their first offseason; Rice#2024 (college) is now fired after its second straight miss instead of after a B season."
  },
  {
   "fp": "5c6292686fc46c87",
   "from": "60ead5ec273d3b91",
   "note": "Gameplans are a real choice: risk makes the rating gap count less on your drives, safe makes it count more, no hidden rating penalty; at even strength all three are worth the same (test/plans.js). Overtime and fourth-down tries keep the old numbers as the engine's own 'urgent' mode, and late-game management its own 'sit'/'chase' modes, so computer-only play is unchanged (college calibration identical; pro realism unchanged). Golden careers answer in-game calls, and 'push'/'protect' now use the new plan modes."
  },
  {
   "fp": "5be87059ba8ecbdc",
   "from": "5c6292686fc46c87",
   "note": "Pro grades: wins against expectation count 0.6, playoff bonuses halved, losing-season penalty 1.25; on 256 seasons A+ 27.7% -> 9.0%, year-to-year swing 3.58 -> 2.95 steps, missed seasons unchanged at ~35%"
  }
